Let $X$ be a Banach space and let $(T(t))_{t\ge 0}$ be a strongly continuous (i.e., $C_0$-) semigroup of bounded linear operators on $X$, with infinitesimal generator $A:D(A)\subseteq X\to X$ defined by
$$Ax=\lim_{t\downarrow 0}\frac{T(t)x-x}{t},\qquad D(A)=\Big\{x\in X:\lim_{t\downarrow 0}\tfrac{T(t)x-x}{t}\text{ exists in }X\Big\}.$$
Consider the following two properties:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] the range $\operatorname{rg}A=\{Ax:x\in D(A)\}$ is closed in $X$;
\item[(ii)] there exists some $t_0>0$ such that the range $\operatorname{rg}(I-T(t_0))$ is closed in $X$.
\end{enumerate}
Does (ii) imply (i)? That is, if $\operatorname{rg}(I-T(t_0))$ is closed for some single $t_0>0$, must $\operatorname{rg}A$ also be closed?

